Wrong kind of puddings. These are not Dutch puddings, they're English
puddings. In English, a pudding is not necessarily a dessert; for
example, the creature under consideration, the black pudding, shares its
name with the dish which in Dutch is called bloedworst. Very much not
vegetarian (and disgusting).
While the word is also, and AFAICT in the USA mostly, used for the
sweet, custardy dessert, the original meaning is the big, fat sausage
one.

